<code>assert \forall int i; i >= 0; this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) || set.get(i));</code>
--------------------
Looking at the comment: after the OR operation, each bit is set if and only if it was already set before OR the corresponding bit in the argument set was set.

This is a biconditional over all bit indices. I'll use `\forall`, the `get` observer, `\old` for the prior state, and `set.get(i)` for the argument's bits.

<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) || set.get(i));</code>
--------------------
Looking at the comment, I need to express that after OR, each bit `i` is set iff it was already set before OR the corresponding bit in `set` was set.

The relevant observer is `get(int bitIndex)`. Using `<==>` style via equality of booleans:

<code>assert \forall int i; i>=0; this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) || set.get(i));</code>
--------------------
